Many thanks Haavard. You were right. Indeed, while tsv2 were integers, they were not the right integers, as they were times in seconds, evaluated every two seconds, and not necessarily starting at 1.

I have re-coded tsv2 to correspond to the integers 1,2,...,n_i, where n_i is the number of observations inside the level i of the random effect, and this error seems to have been solved (i.e. unlike what I had implied in my original post, you don't need the same number of observations inside each level of the random effect, which is sensible)

Now I am struggling with the model outputs, but that is another story unlikely to be useful at this point for the list.

best,

T

