MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The local (or marginal) precision is not the degree of smoothness. If
you think about the degree of differentiability as a degree of
smoothness, any rw1 is equally smooth. You can play with rw2 instead,
which models the second order differences.

Elias

